[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
bsdthinkpad needs some system configuration, which installing does not change.
Run once, as root:

    bsdthinkpad-setup        # or "bsdthinkpad-setup -n" to see the steps first

It loads acpi_ibm and acpi_call (now and in /boot/loader.conf), gives
pkexec's PAM service a session stack without pam_lastlog (whose "Last
login" message makes pkexec abort; the original is kept as
%%PREFIX%%/etc/pam.d/polkit-1.orig), restarts devd for the mic-mute rule
and sets the OSS pcm level to 1.00.

Then log out and in again (bsdthinkpad starts with the session) and add the
panel item "ThinkPad Controls".  Bind the brightness keys to
"bsdthinkpad brightness +10" / "bsdthinkpad brightness -10" in
Settings -> Keyboard -> Application Shortcuts; leave the volume keys to the
PulseAudio plugin.
EOM
}
{ type: remove
  message: <<EOM
bsdthinkpad-setup's changes stay: acpi_ibm_load/acpi_call_load in
/boot/loader.conf and %%PREFIX%%/etc/pam.d/polkit-1 (original in
polkit-1.orig).
EOM
}
]
